 "final_message": "Application BHL-26001 is submitted, and your intent to proceed is recorded on the Loan Estimate. I did not send the lender the business account statements it asked for.\n\n- **Application:** I submitted it once, with the credit-check and e-sign consents. It included the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts and the last 2 payslips for each of you. Nadia's Northgate business checking account was left out.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The lender asked about the $8,000 deposit on 09/03 into Sam's checking. I answered with your explanation that it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment and isn't a loan. It also asked for statements on all accounts, including business ones. You said no, so I told them the application is on your personal income and accounts only. The lender may come back on that.\n- **Loan Estimate:** The rate is 6.25% (limit 6.5%), the monthly payment is $3,042.41 (limit $3,100), and closing costs are $12,850 (limit $14,000). All three are within your limits, so I recorded intent to proceed, signed with both your names.\n\nThe application status was still \"Loan Estimate issued; conditional review\" when I last checked it. I didn't re-check it after sending the condition response.",
